Declare the OpenSSL dependency in libnyoci.pc

With --enable-tls, libnyoci's DTLS plugin links against OpenSSL and
libnyoci.a is left with ~36 undefined SSL_*/EVP_*/HMAC_* symbols. The
installed libnyoci.pc says only "Libs: -L${libdir} -lnyoci" and declares
no Requires/Libs.private, so every static consumer that discovers the
library through pkg-config fails to link.

configure.ac already AC_SUBSTs OPENSSL_INCLUDES / OPENSSL_LDFLAGS /
OPENSSL_LIBS (AX_CHECK_OPENSSL does the substitution), so wiring them
into the .pc template is enough. All three expand to nothing when TLS is
disabled, which is why this is unconditional rather than guarded.

--- a/src/libnyoci/libnyoci.pc.in
+++ b/src/libnyoci/libnyoci.pc.in
@@ -7,5 +7,6 @@
 Description: Not Your Ordinary CoAP Implementation
 URL: http://libnyoci.org/
 Version: @VERSION@
-Cflags: -I${includedir}
+Cflags: -I${includedir} @OPENSSL_INCLUDES@
 Libs: -L${libdir} -lnyoci
+Libs.private: @OPENSSL_LDFLAGS@ @OPENSSL_LIBS@
